# The 1983 source: MERGE of a tokenised file is Bad file mode (DSKCOM.ASM OKGET2), where PC-BASIC reads it as text (Direct statement in file); and more after MERGE's name is Syntax error, the file closed first (MERGE: PRGFIN, SNERR), where PC-BASIC passes it over.
Ok
10 PRINT "ten"
30 PRINT "thirty"
SAVE "LM1",A
Ok
NEW
Ok
20 PRINT "twenty"
30 PRINT "old thirty"
40 PRINT "forty"
MERGE "LM1"
Ok
LIST
10 PRINT "ten"
20 PRINT "twenty"
30 PRINT "thirty"
40 PRINT "forty"
Ok
RUN
ten
twenty
thirty
forty
Ok
SAVE "LM2"
Ok
MERGE "LM2"
Bad file mode
Ok
LIST
10 PRINT "ten"
20 PRINT "twenty"
30 PRINT "thirty"
40 PRINT "forty"
Ok
MERGE "NOFILE"
File not found
Ok
MERGE "LM1",X
Syntax error
Ok
LIST
10 PRINT "ten"
20 PRINT "twenty"
30 PRINT "thirty"
40 PRINT "forty"
Ok
